// Automatic package updates are OFF on this box, deliberately.
//
// This machine's whole job is long-lived Claude sessions: tmux servers and node processes
// that hold conversation state in memory for days. Unattended-upgrades cannot upgrade a
// shared library without needrestart wanting to cycle whatever links it, and on this box
// that is always a session unit. It cost us:
//
//   2026-09-02 06:48 + 06:51  libssh/zlib/util-linux -> claude-restore restarted twice,
//                             all 22 sessions killed, 4 lost for four hours
//   2026-09-03 06:33          ncurses/libgcrypt/libevent -> claude-dashboard-ctl restarted
//                             three times in 22 seconds, two-day dashboard conversation
//                             replaced by an empty session
//
// The needrestart overrides in needrestart/80-claude-sessions.conf and KillMode=process on
// the units are the targeted fixes; this is the blunt one, and it is the only layer that
// also covers a unit nobody has thought to add to that list yet — which is precisely how
// the 2026-09-03 outage happened.
//
// TRADE-OFF: security updates are no longer installed on their own. Patch by hand:
//   sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade
// Do it at a time when killing a session is acceptable, and expect needrestart to ask.
APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists "0";
APT::Periodic::Unattended-Upgrade "0";
APT::Periodic::Download-Upgradeable-Packages "0";
APT::Periodic::AutocleanInterval "0";
